 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the workers' compensation law, in relation to the direct\ndeposit of benefits",
    "basePrintNo": "S7210",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7210-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §25, Work Comp L",
    "lawSection": "Workers' Compensation Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7210\n\nSPONSOR: SAVINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the workers' compensation law, in relation to the direct\ndeposit of benefits\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 9 of section 25 of the workers' compen-\nsation law to allow for direct deposit of workers compensation benefits,\nto allow those benefits to be split among different accounts and to have\nthe Workers Compensation Board promulgate such notice and forms neces-\nsary to allow for direct deposit\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently, the Workers' Compensation Law regarding the direct deposit of\nbenefits states that insurance carriers may provide direct deposit bene-\nfits to injured workers and persons receiving death benefits. The\ncurrent language of the statute only permits insurance carrier to have\nthe option of direct deposit. This does not mandate the carriers to\nprovide this service to workers who receive these vital benefits and\ncompensation. There are injured workers and persons who receive death\nbenefits that appeal to their insurance carriers, which are largely the\nfor-profit insurance carriers that handle workers' compensation insur-\nance benefits in New York. State, for direct deposit and they are told\nthat the carrier does not provide direct deposit. This is an issue that\nadds hardship to those Injured workers and persons receiving death bene-\nfits.\n\nThis bill mandates that insurance carriers provide direct deposit insur-\nance to injured workers and persons receiving death benefits.  Also,\nthis bill ensures that the Workers' Compensation Board provides informa-\ntion about direct deposit to eligible persons and the appropriate\ndocumentation to allow them. to file for direct deposit of their\nbenefits/compensation. Lastly, this bill specifically allows the eligi-\nble to have their compensation/benefits deposited by dollar amount or\npercentage. The Board is given the opportunity promulgate rules\nsurrounding the implementation of this legislation.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
